    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d903">

                <pb facs="0854" n="848" xml:id="pg848"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890D.1124 Bitzer, John Andre/6: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bullitt</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-11-08T17:00:00+00:00">November 8, 1939—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 5:24 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2690. Your 1313, October 26, 6 p.m. Foreign Office upon Embassy’s request has
                    taken up the John Andre Bitzer case with the authorities at Beirut and is
                    awaiting a reply.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bullitt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
